<title>FRANCE: Hot, dry weather ideal for French beet growth.</title>
<headline>Hot, dry weather ideal for French beet growth.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hot and dry weather over France in the past two weeks has been perfect for the sugar beet crop, planters said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The beets are doing well. Hot weather is good for plant growth and there is no concern over lack of moisture as the beets got plenty of rain in June and July,&quot; an analyst for the French sugar beet planters federation (CGB) told Reuters.</p>
<p>He also said a few scattered thunderstorms were bringing beets some relief from scorching temperatures, particularly in central France.</p>
</text>
